From 0b038edb99abc8543f59a772a2b7db95291ae55f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:32:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Gui: the stereo fit's pixel distances in a function of their
 own, with a unit test

The distances the stereo 3D view keeps inside the person's limits are now
computed from the measuring pass's pictures by stereoFitDistances()
(View3DStereoFit), with the meaning they had: each pixel at the depth of its
nearest surface, the scene's and the annotations'.  The unit test
View3DStereoFit (Gui_tests_run) states the rule the next change builds: a
pixel counts at the contribution-weighted mean distance of what it shows.
On this commit its translucent, annotation and unfogged cases fail.

Forwarded: not-needed (FreeCAD's AI_POLICY.md and AGENTS.md; the edition's build)
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
